  "worked_solution": "The rate of change in the temperature $T$ of the object is given by $\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nWe are told that the temperature *decreases* at a rate that is equal to $0.03$ times $(T-25).$ Therefore, the corresponding differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-0.03(T-25).\n$$",
